Z||000000||Hank is Here||10-11-2001||12:34 PM||||Was there ever a 86/87 SE made with the V6 and 5 speed.  I ask because it seems that every SE I see out there is an auto.  Heck for that matter was there an 86 V6 4 speed?  <P>anyone have one?   ||||reg||1
Z||000001||JetroGT||10-11-2001||12:37 PM||||Yes. I've seen 86 and 87 SE V6's with 5spds.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||mrfiero||10-11-2001||12:54 PM||||I've owned both an '86SE and an '87 SE with a V-6 & 5-sp.  They are somewhat "rare".....the vast majority of stickshift '86 SE's were 4-speeds and very few '87 SE's were even built, so the number of '86-'87 SE V-6 5-sp. cars built is very small.<P><BR>They're out there though, so if you want one keep looking.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||88CoupeV6||10-11-2001||02:47 PM||||Most 86 SE's I've seen have a 4 speed.<P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/newsig.jpg">    <BR>:D  <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Old Lar||10-11-2001||02:53 PM||||87 models were the first to have the Getrag 5 speed transmission except for the few 86 GT's that had the new 5 speeds put in during late production run of the 86.<BR>So I would expect that any 87 SE V6 that had a manual transmission, it was a 5 speed.||||reg||1
